    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the route deviation is established, but the traffic question this case turns on cannot be answered on this record, so the fare is held and the case goes to a human reviewer.\n\nThe deviation. On the platform's own recorded distances (EV-TRIP-05009) the trip ran 10.0 km against a recommended 8.5 km, so under POL-RD-22 the deviation is 1.50 km — 0.50 km beyond the 1.0 km tolerance, and well below POL-RD-25's 2.0 km ceiling, so the AI could in principle rule on the deviation itself. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-05009) shows which route was taken and when (BKE left at Woodlands Avenue 2, Woodlands Road, rejoin at Petir Road) but under POL-RD-22 it is not used to re-measure distance.\n\nThe obstacle. POL-RD-24's matrix turns on whether the reroute was traffic-justified. The only artifact that could carry that fact is the LTA traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05009-01, and it is MISSING — weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (the platform's feed request for this trip window timed out and was not retried). Under POL-GEN-02 a MISSING artifact carries no fact, and the record is silent on traffic: it is not a finding that the BKE was clear. POL-RD-23 requires positive traffic data to justify a reroute, and a driver's assertion alone does not justify it. POL-GEN-26 names 'whether traffic justified the reroute' among the facts that must go to a human reviewer when the evidence that would carry it is missing or impaired. The traffic limb is therefore undecided: it supports neither a refund that needs justification to fail nor the driver's position that needs it to hold.\n\nThe rider's points. The 1.50 km deviation is accepted. The arithmetic is accepted too — the excess distance fare would be 1.50 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.08 SGD on EV-FARE-05009 (fare charged 14.05 SGD; refund issued so far 0.0). But the claim that the reroute is 'not traffic-justified' cannot be used: its only carrier is the missing advisory at weight 0.0, so a ruling